Title: [ROM][UNOFFICIAL][17][cheetah] Evolution X 12.3 (Android 17) for the Pixel 7 Pro - testers wanted
After posting: set cheetah's FORUM in evolution-kodiak/tools/p11-ota.sh to the thread URL (server copy too).

[CENTER][SIZE=6][B]Evolution X 12.3 — Android 17[/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4]Google Pixel 7 Pro (cheetah) | UNOFFICIAL | TEST BUILD[/SIZE][/CENTER]

[CODE]
/*
 * Your warranty is now void. You flash this at your own risk.
 * I'm not responsible for bricked devices, lost data, or anything else.
 */
[/CODE]

[SIZE=5][B]Testers wanted: this build has never been booted[/B][/SIZE]
I build Evolution X for the Pixel 11 series and run it daily on a Pixel 11 Pro XL. This is [B]Evolution X 12.3 on Android 17 for the Pixel 7 Pro (cheetah)[/B], built from Evolution X's own Pixel 7 device trees. It passes every check I can run without the phone, but [B]it has never been booted.[/B] Only try it if you're comfortable restoring stock with the Android Flash Tool if it doesn't boot.

If you try it, please reply in this thread with:
[LIST]
[*]Whether it boots, and whether it still boots after a couple of reboots
[*]Your carrier, and whether calls, SMS, VoLTE, mobile data and Wi-Fi calling work
[*]Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, cameras, fingerprint and face unlock
[*]Play Integrity and Google Wallet
[*]If something fails: what you saw, and a log if you can get one ([ICODE]adb logcat -d > logcat.txt[/ICODE])
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]About[/B][/SIZE]
An [B]unofficial[/B] build of Evolution X 12.3 on Android 17 for the Pixel 7 Pro. The Pixel 7 Pro has an official Evolution X maintainer for Android 16 (nhansp); Evolution X hasn't released official Android 17 builds for it yet. When it does, switch to the official builds. Ours are signed with different keys, so moving between the two needs a clean flash.

[B]For the Pixel 7 Pro (cheetah) only.[/B] Don't flash it on the Pixel 7 (panther) or any other model.

This is [B]not[/B] an official Evolution X build. Please don't report its bugs to the Evolution X team; report them in this thread.

[SIZE=5][B]Build info[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Evolution X 12.3, Android 17, security patch {SYSTEM_SPL} (system), {VENDOR_SPL} (vendor)
[*]Build type: user, signed with private release keys
[*]Google apps included
[*]Device trees and blobs: Evolution X's own (device_google_pantah, device_google_gs201, vendor_google_cheetah)
[*]Kernel: LineageOS's gs201 kernel (Linux 6.1), built from source with the ROM
[*]Over-the-air updates through the built-in Updater; they include Google's firmware {FIRMWARE}
[*]Not rooted
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]What should work[/B][/SIZE]
Evolution X's Pixel 7 trees have a long record on Android 16, but none of this is confirmed on this Android 17 build yet:
[LIST]
[*]Calls and SMS, including VoLTE, mobile data, eSIM
[*]Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, NFC
[*]Cameras, fingerprint (under-display), face unlock
[*]Google Play; Play Integrity and Google Wallet tap-to-pay
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]Known issues[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Untested on real hardware (see above).
[*]Gemini Nano and the features built on it don't work. Google only serves the on-device AI models to phones with a locked bootloader, so this applies to any custom ROM.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]Requirements[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Unlocked bootloader (unlocking wipes your phone)
[*]Google's stock firmware [B]{FIRMWARE}[/B] or newer. The zip doesn't flash a bootloader or radio, so install the latest Android 17 factory image for the Pixel 7 Pro with the Android Flash Tool first. Later updates through the Updater keep the firmware current.
[*]Latest platform-tools (adb/fastboot)
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]Installation (clean flash)[/B][/SIZE]
Download the ROM zip and check its SHA-256, then:
[CODE]
adb reboot bootloader
fastboot -w update {FASTBOOT_ZIP}
[/CODE]
[B]-w wipes all your data.[/B] fastboot switches to fastbootd partway through to flash the dynamic partitions; leave the phone plugged in until it reboots by itself (a few minutes). The first boot takes a few minutes more.

[SIZE=5][B]Downloads[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]ROM zip and OTA package: [URL=https://sourceforge.net/projects/denson9874-s-user-builds/files/cheetah/17/]SourceForge: cheetah/17[/URL]
[*]SHA-256 checksums: in the same folder ({FASTBOOT_SHA256})
[/LIST]

